{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And the people cried out to Moses.</b> And not to HaShem — for they thought that since Moses had not yet taken notice of their sin, he would suppose that what happened to them was a chance occurrence and would pray on their behalf. And so Moses did, supposing that the place caused it — for there are places on earth where a great wind lies hidden, causing a trembling of the earth, and there are places where fire lies hidden. Therefore Moses called the name of the place Taberah, for he thought that the place caused it and not their sin."], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:40:33.636481766Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}